    "result_text": "Owner responses now include a `checkDigit` field: the Luhn check digit worked out from the digits in `customerCode`. I ran the full test suite and all 10 tests pass, including the new check-digit acceptance test.\n\n- **API spec** (`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`): I added `checkDigit` to the `Owner` schema as a read-only whole number from 0 to 9. The response class that the endpoints return is generated from this file, so the field shows up there automatically.\n- **Mapping** (`OwnerMapper.java`): a new `toCheckDigit(owner)` method calculates the digit, and `toOwnerDto` now uses it. It skips letters and dashes, so for `MAD-FRA-0002` it only uses `0002`, which gives 6. It returns nothing when an owner has no customer code, the same way `membershipNumber` already behaves.\n\nThe digit is worked out each time an owner is returned rather than saved, so there are no database changes. Owners that already exist get a check digit too.",
